cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these results or tools, please cite them as below."
title: "Szilassi polyhedra: every seven-hexagon torus without overarching faces has exactly one convex face, and no symmetric 12-face Szilassi polyhedron exists (computer-assisted proofs with DRAT certificates)"
authors:
  - name: "Moki & Julio"
date-released: 2026-10-16
version: "1.1"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23003257
repository-code: "https://github.com/Hashirama1337s/szilassi-12"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - Szilassi polyhedron
  - polyhedral torus
  - hexangulation
  - convex faces
  - neighbourly polyhedra
  - oriented matroids
  - SAT
  - DRAT proof
  - computer-assisted proof
abstract: >-
  Part A (v1.1): every acoptic polyhedral torus with seven hexagonal faces and no overarching faces has exactly one
  convex face, so Conjecture 5.7 of Grünbaum and Szilassi (2009), that every hexangulation of the torus has at least
  six non-convex faces, holds with equality in this case. Two independently written oriented-matroid SAT encodings give
  UNSAT for "at least two convex faces" and for "no convex face", each with a DRAT proof verified by drat-trim;
  Szilassi's published coordinates are checked exactly. Part B (v1.0): no polyhedron with 12 faces in which every two
  faces share an edge has a non-trivial symmetry (36 SAT instances, all UNSAT with verified DRAT proofs).
